WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
Real SMB. Real files.
SmartNAS → Python service → Mac browser

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.800
Install once
Python + pipx already installed

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.800
Installed from PyPI
The published 0.2.1 package

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:09.520
Sign in from another device
Demo connection: SSH over Tailscale

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.800
Scan your LAN
Choose the subnet the service should probe

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.000
Real network results
SMB and NFS services discovered on the LAN

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.800
Switch subnet
Select 192.168.122.0/24 — the NAT VM network

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.760
Subnet scan complete
No SMB/NFS services replied on this VM subnet

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.760
Map a real SMB server
SmartNAS at 192.168.0.107

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.440
Save SMB credentials
Authenticate and list the server’s shares

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.040
SMB connected
Open the dedicated remotefs-demo share

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:35.120
Save a network location
Add the repository folder to your shortlist

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.160
Read files from the NAS
Preview the remote repository’s README

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.640
Browse the Python source
Open src/remote_fs_browser/cli.py over SMB

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.920
Shift-click a range
Select several files in one action

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.040
Right-click for file actions
Choose Download from the context menu

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.320
Download over SMB
The file streams through the service to this Mac

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:56.120
SMB proof
Downloaded bytes matched the NAS source

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.120
Saved locations persist
Reload and reopen the network folder

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:02.800
Reconnect with saved credentials
Map the server without retyping the password

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.320
Unmount the connection
Session deleted; no operating-system mount was created

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:10.320
Open a browser from another device, from anywhere.
One service, wherever your permitted connection can reach it
